WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:04.925
Welcome to another Famous Friday

00:00:05.186 --> 00:00:06.941
where we look at famous entrepreneurs

00:00:07.203 --> 00:00:10.734
and help you model their success to help your business grow.

00:00:11.179 --> 00:00:13.377
Today’s lesson is Show Me.

00:00:14.103 --> 00:00:15.298
If you have a new idea

00:00:15.494 --> 00:00:17.690
a new concept, something that’s revolutionary

00:00:17.862 --> 00:00:19.059
something that’s going to change the world

00:00:19.978 --> 00:00:22.305
then you need to show me how it works.

00:00:22.466 --> 00:00:24.262
Don’t just come to me with a piece of paper

00:00:24.763 --> 00:00:26.617
or a PowerPoint file or an email

00:00:26.987 --> 00:00:28.986
and say, “Here’s the blueprint, here’s how it’s going to work…”

00:00:29.247 --> 00:00:31.295
Show me it’s working!

00:00:31.671 --> 00:00:33.099
Because the bigger the idea is

00:00:33.265 --> 00:00:34.819
the more unique it is, the newer it is

00:00:35.027 --> 00:00:38.483
the more people are going to be skeptical that it’s going to work.

00:00:39.535 --> 00:00:41.472
So instead of just trying to sell them with an email

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.326
or a PowerPoint presentation

00:00:43.685 --> 00:00:48.509
sell them by actually showing them how your product or service works.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:51.201
So one of my favorite examples is from Henry Ford.

00:00:51.688 --> 00:00:53.999
Henry Ford, founder of the Ford Motor Company

00:00:54.322 --> 00:00:55.323
legendary entrepreneur.

00:00:55.789 --> 00:00:57.646
When he first started he was an engineer.

00:00:58.116 --> 00:01:00.050
He was an engineer at Edison Electrical

00:01:00.342 --> 00:01:02.730
and was helping create electricity for America.

00:01:03.221 --> 00:01:04.947
And he wanted to do his own thing

00:01:05.092 --> 00:01:06.220
you know, he wanted to be an entrepreneur.

00:01:06.416 --> 00:01:09.175
He had ideas too. He didn’t want to just work for somebody else.

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:12.049
And so he wanted to get into the car business

00:01:12.359 --> 00:01:14.118
and the car business was super new,

00:01:14.281 --> 00:01:15.358
nobody was really making cars

00:01:15.619 --> 00:01:18.297
a whole bunch of engineers just creating their own inventions.

00:01:18.974 --> 00:01:20.702
And so he came up with his own invention

00:01:20.962 --> 00:01:22.349
and he called it the Quadricycle.

00:01:22.918 --> 00:01:25.273
And the quadricycle was basically two bicycles

00:01:25.743 --> 00:01:28.959
that were attached together with a gasoline engine in the middle

00:01:29.197 --> 00:01:32.511
and that was one of the very first cars in America

00:01:32.673 --> 00:01:33.703
it was this primitive design.

00:01:34.103 --> 00:01:35.479
And he wanted to get funding for this

00:01:35.652 --> 00:01:37.691
and he wanted to quit his job and he wanted to go

00:01:37.853 --> 00:01:39.888
and create a company building quadricycles.

00:01:40.519 --> 00:01:42.862
And it was such a new, crazy idea, you know.

00:01:42.862 --> 00:01:44.452
People are used to riding horses.

00:01:44.778 --> 00:01:48.395
“Why would I ride this contraption quadricycle thing?”

00:01:48.928 --> 00:01:51.914
And so instead of just going out and pitching people on…

00:01:52.448 --> 00:01:54.144
with the perspectives on paper,

00:01:54.738 --> 00:01:56.902
what he did was he built his first quadricycle.

00:01:57.194 --> 00:01:58.665
And he wanted to go to William Murphy

00:01:59.193 --> 00:02:02.455
who was a highly successful entrepreneur in the lumber business.

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:06.767
And when he went to pitch him he showed up in his quadricycle

00:02:06.963 --> 00:02:10.060
a working quadricycle prototype unit

00:02:10.429 --> 00:02:12.856
and he took William Murphy for a ride on it around town

00:02:13.159 --> 00:02:16.869
and by the end of the ride they were in business together.

00:02:17.178 --> 00:02:18.032
That’s how it works!

00:02:18.329 --> 00:02:21.947
It’s so much easier to convince people to give you money

00:02:22.085 --> 00:02:23.139
to buy from you

00:02:23.285 --> 00:02:25.901
to refer people to you, to put you in the media

00:02:26.271 --> 00:02:27.900
to have you be guest on their shows

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:29.191
whatever it is you’re looking for

00:02:29.385 --> 00:02:33.052
it’s so much easier for people to understand what you do

00:02:33.439 --> 00:02:35.570
when they can experience it

00:02:36.039 --> 00:02:39.219
when you’re not just talking about it but they can feel it.

00:02:39.458 --> 00:02:43.144
And so if you want to sell your idea, you want to get investors

00:02:43.611 --> 00:02:44.579
you want to get customers

00:02:44.741 --> 00:02:47.467
you want to get momentum then show me.

00:02:48.098 --> 00:02:49.956
Make me feel it.

00:02:50.776 --> 00:02:51.834
Believe.

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:53.910
For those of you watching, you like this video

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:56.494
you can support me by clicking on the link in the description.

00:02:56.789 --> 00:02:58.291
Leave a comment. Let me know what you think.

00:02:58.462 --> 00:03:00.806
And click on my face to subscribe to the channel.

00:03:00.951 --> 00:03:03.046
Thank you so much, I’ll see you soon.

